  "verdict": {
    "verdict": "C (genuinely-open) with a clean B (production-wrong) sub-finding",
    "summary": "The q-volume functional, as the framework defines it (def:algebraic-quantum-volume + thm:markov-trace-product + prop:vol-through-tau), is Vol_q(beta)=tr_M(rho(beta)) followed by tau_arch = ln|.| at q0. tau_arch is a LOGARITHM, not a multiplicative factor, so a 2.38x multiplicative bridge is the wrong shape. No zero-parameter functional of tr_M reproduces the production scalar (closest tr_M^2 at -55%). prop:vol-through-tau says Vol(B3)=ln|tr_M|=-0.00144, but production uses classical 8G=7.328 -- two volume definitions inconsistent by ~5090x at q0. Not (A): wrong shape, no zero-param match, A-vs-B inconsistent.",
    "not_A_reasons": [
      "tau_arch is ln|.| (logarithm), not multiplicative",
      "no zero-parameter q-vol functional of tr_M matches (>=55% off)",
      "classical Vol=8G vs prop:vol-through-tau Vol=ln|tr_M| disagree ~5090x at q0"
    ],
